WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.596
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Intermediate.

2
00:00:04.896 --> 00:00:07.957
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.257 --> 00:00:14.311
Unit eleven: Protecting the Environment. In this unit, you will talk about environmental problems and solutions.

4
00:00:15.317 --> 00:00:16.631
renewable energy.

5
00:00:17.331 --> 00:00:22.013
renewable energy means energy from sources that don't run out, like the sun and wind.

6
00:00:22.313 --> 00:00:25.369
Cambodia is building more renewable energy projects.

7
00:00:26.069 --> 00:00:28.849
Your turn. Say: renewable energy.

8
00:00:31.549 --> 00:00:33.258
renewable energy.

9
00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:35.599
single-use plastic.

10
00:00:36.299 --> 00:00:40.586
single-use plastic means plastic that is used once and then thrown away.

11
00:00:40.886 --> 00:00:44.267
Many cafés no longer give single-use plastic straws.

12
00:00:44.967 --> 00:00:48.061
Your turn. Say: single-use plastic.

13
00:00:50.761 --> 00:00:52.424
single-use plastic.

14
00:00:53.417 --> 00:00:54.557
recycle bin.

15
00:00:55.257 --> 00:00:58.545
recycle bin means a container for things that can be recycled.

16
00:00:58.845 --> 00:01:00.891
Please put bottles in the recycle bin.

17
00:01:01.591 --> 00:01:03.965
Your turn. Say: recycle bin.

18
00:01:06.665 --> 00:01:07.863
recycle bin.

19
00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:10.234
wildlife habitat.

20
00:01:10.934 --> 00:01:14.083
wildlife habitat means the natural home of wild animals.

21
00:01:14.383 --> 00:01:17.161
Cutting down forests destroys wildlife habitat.

22
00:01:17.861 --> 00:01:20.501
Your turn. Say: wildlife habitat.

23
00:01:23.201 --> 00:01:24.864
wildlife habitat.

24
00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:27.130
eco-friendly product.

25
00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:31.408
eco-friendly product means a product that does not harm the environment.

26
00:01:31.708 --> 00:01:35.519
Bamboo toothbrushes are a popular eco-friendly product.

27
00:01:36.219 --> 00:01:38.987
Your turn. Say: eco-friendly product.

28
00:01:41.687 --> 00:01:43.141
eco-friendly product.

29
00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:45.105
landfill.

30
00:01:45.805 --> 00:01:48.930
landfill means a place where rubbish is buried in the ground.

31
00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:52.054
Most plastic ends up in a landfill or the ocean.

32
00:01:52.754 --> 00:01:55.244
Your turn. Say: landfill.

33
00:01:57.944 --> 00:01:58.980
landfill.

34
00:01:59.983 --> 00:02:01.112
compost bin.

35
00:02:01.812 --> 00:02:05.983
compost bin means a container where food waste turns into soil.

36
00:02:06.283 --> 00:02:08.909
We put vegetable peels in our compost bin.

37
00:02:09.609 --> 00:02:11.995
Your turn. Say: compost bin.

38
00:02:14.695 --> 00:02:15.951
compost bin.

39
00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:18.032
water shortage.

40
00:02:18.732 --> 00:02:21.916
water shortage means a situation when there is not enough water.

41
00:02:22.216 --> 00:02:25.156
Many villages face a water shortage in the dry season.

42
00:02:25.856 --> 00:02:28.578
Your turn. Say: water shortage.

43
00:02:31.278 --> 00:02:32.511
water shortage.

44
00:02:33.517 --> 00:02:35.505
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:35.805 --> 00:02:38.141
I'm worried about all the plastic in the rivers.

46
00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:44.494
Me too. If we don't stop using single-use plastic, it will get worse.

47
00:02:45.783 --> 00:02:47.110
What can we do at home?

48
00:02:48.417 --> 00:02:52.390
If you use a compost bin, you'll send much less waste to the landfill.

49
00:02:53.683 --> 00:02:56.879
And unless people recycle, the problem won't go away.

50
00:02:58.183 --> 00:03:01.950
Exactly. Small changes will help if everyone joins in.

51
00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:06.701
Grammar focus: First conditional + unless.

52
00:03:07.001 --> 00:03:10.440
Use the first conditional for real possibilities in the future.

53
00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:14.518
If plus present simple, then will plus verb. Unless means if not.

54
00:03:14.818 --> 00:03:18.850
For example: Unless we act now, the rivers will become dirtier.

55
00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:23.611
Don't use will after if or unless: say 'If it rains', not 'If it will rain'.

56
00:03:24.617 --> 00:03:27.315
Now read and listen. The Plastic Problem.

57
00:03:27.615 --> 00:03:31.008
Every year, millions of tonnes of plastic enter the world's oceans.

58
00:03:32.317 --> 00:03:36.418
Much of it is single-use plastic, such as bags, cups and straws.

59
00:03:37.717 --> 00:03:42.990
If nothing changes, there will be more plastic than fish in the sea by 2050.

60
00:03:44.283 --> 00:03:48.140
Some cities in Cambodia have started banning plastic bags in markets.

61
00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:54.329
Unless we reduce, reuse and recycle, wildlife habitat will continue to disappear.

62
00:03:55.617 --> 00:03:58.014
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:58.314 --> 00:04:00.592
Energy from the sun and wind is blank.

64
00:04:00.892 --> 00:04:05.021
A, renewable energy. B, landfill. C, water shortage.

65
00:04:09.017 --> 00:04:11.283
The answer is A: renewable energy.

66
00:04:12.783 --> 00:04:15.003
If we blank trees, the city will be cooler.

67
00:04:15.303 --> 00:04:18.411
A, will plant. B, plant. C, planted.

68
00:04:22.417 --> 00:04:24.056
The answer is B: plant.

69
00:04:25.550 --> 00:04:27.782
blank you hurry, you will miss the bus.

70
00:04:28.082 --> 00:04:30.864
A, If. B, Unless. C, When.

71
00:04:34.850 --> 00:04:36.884
The answer is B: Unless.

72
00:04:38.383 --> 00:04:40.894
A place where rubbish is buried is a blank.

73
00:04:41.194 --> 00:04:44.998
A, compost bin. B, landfill. C, recycle bin.

74
00:04:48.983 --> 00:04:50.786
The answer is B: landfill.

75
00:04:52.283 --> 00:04:55.734
According to the text, what may happen by 2050?

76
00:04:56.034 --> 00:05:00.756
A, no more plastic. B, more plastic than fish. C, clean oceans.

77
00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:07.272
The answer is B: more plastic than fish.

78
00:05:08.783 --> 00:05:12.562
Now it's your turn to speak. What will you do to help the environment this year?

79
00:05:17.862 --> 00:05:24.099
If I go shopping, I will always bring my own bag, and I will start a compost bin at home.

80
00:05:24.399 --> 00:05:25.992
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:26.983 --> 00:05:31.633
Great work today! You learned eight new words and first conditional + unless.

82
00:05:31.933 --> 00:05:36.129
Today's value is caring for nature. Care for plants, birds and our planet.

83
00:05:36.429 --> 00:05:38.571
See you in Unit twelve. Goodbye!

84
00:05:38.871 --> 00:05:41.848
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

